WEBVTT

00:02.200 --> 00:04.593
Every app starts as an idea.

00:08.400 --> 00:11.488
OpenWiz asks you a few sharp questions,

00:12.300 --> 00:14.892
and turns your answers into a spec.

00:16.100 --> 00:18.411
The spec splits into tickets.

00:19.200 --> 00:21.045
Then you summon the fleet.

00:24.300 --> 00:26.148
One agent per ticket.

00:27.300 --> 00:29.402
They build at the same time.

00:31.000 --> 00:33.710
A second agent reviews every ticket.

00:34.800 --> 00:36.784
Approved work merges.

00:38.400 --> 00:40.121
And your app ships.

00:42.200 --> 00:45.200
You made the decisions. The fleet did the rest.

00:45.200 --> 00:46.905
So how does it work?

00:47.100 --> 00:50.066
OpenWiz is the kernel: small and open.

00:50.066 --> 00:55.336
GitHub is the ship's log: every spec, ticket and review is a GitHub record.

00:56.500 --> 01:01.331
Drivers pick the sea: your laptop, boat.dev, Cloudroom, or your own.

01:01.331 --> 01:05.986
Harnesses are your crew: Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and more.

01:06.000 --> 01:11.277
WizSkills is the spellbook: grill, to spec, to tickets, build, review.

01:11.277 --> 01:13.300
Plain files your agents read.

01:13.300 --> 01:16.847
WizPlugins bring OpenWiz into the tools you use.

01:16.847 --> 01:20.553
WizBar is your lookout: every ticket at a glance.

01:20.800 --> 01:24.774
The app shows your specs, tickets and agents, straight from GitHub.

01:24.774 --> 01:27.250
Next: a feed of spec videos.

01:28.300 --> 01:31.790
WizRoom is the war room: the factory's scoreboard.

01:31.790 --> 01:33.642
It's private, for now.

01:35.800 --> 01:41.725
And coming soon: WizMarket, a public marketplace where anything in the agent economy can list.

01:41.725 --> 01:43.263
Open to all.

01:45.300 --> 01:47.984
OpenWiz. Bring your own everything.
